<!--
	KitsuneTerrainFit settings (server-side).

	enabled = fit newly placed cubes to the terrain around them.
	          "false" leaves placement fully vanilla. The `tfit refit` console
	          command still works either way.

	alsoFit = blocks to fit even though they aren't plain six-sided cubes,
	          as long as their walls hide the ground tucked inside them.
	          Comma separated block names; * matches anything. Farm plots by
	          default. Set alsoFit="" to fit only plain cubes.

	alsoFitHeight = how far up an alsoFit block the ground may come, as a
	          fraction of its height. 0.75 keeps the ground nearly flush with
	          a farm plot's rim while staying under its soil. 1 would bury the
	          soil; 0.5 or less turns the fill off.

	hillside = how cubes on slopes and in hill cuts are fitted.
	          "embed": filled to the ground around them, so the hill washes
	                   over the uphill edge and they look sunk into the slope.
	          "clear": the ground never rises over a cube's top edge, and cubes
	                   against a cut in the hill are left vanilla.
	          Farm plots always keep their rim clear either way.

	shapes = what happens around upright shapes that aren't plain cubes:
	          rounded corners, pillars, quarter rounds, poles.
	          "keep":    on level ground they're fitted like a cube; anywhere
	                     else they keep the ground density their space already
	                     had, so the ground doesn't dip into a trench around
	                     them. Cubes next to them follow the same rule.
	          "vanilla": only cubes and alsoFit blocks are touched.
	          Steps, ramps, plates and shapes lying on their side are always
	          vanilla: ground at its natural height would poke through them.

	verbose = also log every placement that was looked at and skipped, with
	          the reason. Off by default; fitted blocks are always logged.
	          Can be flipped at runtime with `tfit verbose on|off`.

	Edit and restart the server. If this file is missing or unreadable the
	mod falls back to enabled="true" alsoFit="farmPlotBlock*" alsoFitHeight="0.75" hillside="embed" shapes="keep" verbose="false".
-->
<KitsuneTerrainFit enabled="true" alsoFit="farmPlotBlock*" alsoFitHeight="0.75" hillside="embed" shapes="keep" verbose="false" />
